NAME
       vipw, vigr - safely edit the password and group files

SYNOPSIS
       vipw [-s]
       vigr [-s]

DESCRIPTION
       vipw opens /etc/passwd in an editor ($VISUAL, $EDITOR, or vi), and
       vigr opens /etc/group. They lock the file while you edit, so that
       useradd, passwd and other tools cannot change it at the same moment,
       and they put your copy in place only when you save. With -s they edit
       /etc/shadow or /etc/gshadow instead. After editing one, they offer to
       edit the matching shadow file too.

       Prefer useradd, usermod, groupmod and gpasswd; use vipw and vigr only
       for changes those cannot make. Only root can run them.

OPTIONS
       -s     Edit the shadow file.

EXAMPLES
           vipw
           vigr

SEE ALSO
       passwd(5), group(5), shadow(5), usermod(8), pwck(8), grpck(8)
